deployed: 2026-05-11T09:00:00Z · v1.0.45 (Desktop avatar Enter clicks at AVATAR position, not cursor — previously the v1.0.10 Enter handler used _cursor.x/y (mouse position) for elementFromPoint, so pressing Enter while the avatar was somewhere else clicked the wrong target. Now reads the avatar's bounding rect via canvas[data-cr-os-invader] and clicks at the avatar's center; mouse cursor irrelevant. Added _avatarCenter() helper. Avatar canvas is hidden during the elementFromPoint call so it doesn't steal the hit-test from the underlying target.)
